id: pm-4s24d2
title: Release pipeline permits duplicate same-day production versions
description: "Close the release-policy enforcement gap that allowed three 2026.7.24 tags and two npm publications. Remove the local same-day ordinal bypass, fail closed on legacy override attempts, require a single calendar version per UTC day, document same-tag partial-release recovery, and prove the invariant with unit, integration, workflow-contract, and isolated manual tests."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[4]: automation,regression,release,security
created_at: "2026-07-24T15:16:37.435Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T15:45:27.659Z"
assignee: codex-root-agent
author: codex-root-agent
acceptance_criteria: The release preparation pipeline cannot create an ordinal same-day production version; Any existing UTC-day release tag yields release_already_cut_today before mutation; Legacy same-day override requests fail closed with actionable same-tag recovery guidance; Release documentation explains retrying the existing tag after partial npm or GitHub failures
parent: pm-u9d0
