comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T15:16:37.435Z",codex-root-agent,"Duplicate check: searched all statuses for multiple same-day releases, ordinal auto release, and allow-same-day-release; no open canonical defect exists. Related completed incidents pm-cedo0g and pm-gis0qo repaired downstream failures but exposed the still-live pipeline bypass; recurring verification item pm-7zs0 and policy decision pm-ee1k provide lineage."
  "2026-07-24T15:21:09.593Z",codex-root-agent,"TDD evidence: the focused 55-test unit/integration/workflow contract set failed against the retained bypass, then passed after removing ordinal generation, rejecting the legacy override before Git inspection, and routing blocker recovery to the exact existing tag workflow."
  "2026-07-24T15:38:27.009Z",codex-root-agent,"Verification evidence: 355 files / 6,222 tests passed with repository-wide 100% statements (42,725/42,725), branches (30,306/30,306), functions (8,704/8,704), and lines (41,527/41,527). Focused pipeline coverage is independently 100/100/100/100. Static quality, ESLint, jscpd (0 clones), CodeFactor complexity, docstrings (100%), token budgets, package boundary, docs/skills links, TypeScript, secret scan, YAML parse, extracted workflow ShellCheck, compatibility migration, npm pack dry-run, and the 88-command packed package dogfood all passed."
  "2026-07-24T15:45:27.659Z",codex-root-agent,"GitHub linkage: PR #674 implements the fix; closed blocker issue #664 now links back to this canonical PM item and records the root-cause distinction from the downstream Bun and npm dist-tag incidents."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T15:16:37.435Z",codex-root-agent,"Incident snapshot 2026-07-24 UTC: v2026.7.24, v2026.7.24-2, and v2026.7.24-3 tags exist; npm published 2026.7.24 and 2026.7.24-3. The base Release run failed after npm publication, -2 failed during npm publication, and -3 completed. Recovery should have retried the existing tag instead of cutting new ordinal versions."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T15:16:37.435Z",codex-root-agent,Removing the workflow input alone is insufficient when the reusable local release pipeline retains the same production bypass. The invariant must be enforced at the lowest mutation-capable boundary.
  "2026-07-24T15:38:27.629Z",codex-root-agent,"Partial-release recovery has two distinct phases: before a tag exists, rerun preparation; after a tag exists, rerun the exact immutable tag workflow. Conflating these phases is what allowed ordinal recovery releases and could also close a blocker without repairing the original tag."
